                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A charming little adventure with a lot of heart! ⚔️✨\n\nPankapu is one of those games that immediately caught my attention with its colorful art style and charming presentation, but what really kept me playing was how enjoyable the actual gameplay is.\n\nIt's a fun action-platformer with a great mixture of exploration, combat, platforming, upgrades, and a surprisingly interesting story.\n\nIt has that classic feeling of picking up a game and thinking, \"I'll play for a little while,\" only to realize you've been playing for much longer than expected. 😂\n\n⚔️ Fun and satisfying combat\n\nThe combat is simple enough to understand quickly, but there's enough variety to keep things interesting.\n\nPankapu has different abilities and combat styles that allow you to approach situations in different ways. Switching between them depending on what you're fighting adds a nice bit of variety to the gameplay.\n\nEnemies are also varied enough that you can't simply use the exact same strategy throughout the entire game.\n\nSometimes you need to attack aggressively.\n\nSometimes you need to avoid incoming attacks.\n\nAnd sometimes the best strategy is simply hit everything before it has a chance to hit you. 😂\n\n🌈 The world looks fantastic\n\nThe visual style is easily one of the game's biggest strengths.\n\nEverything is colorful, imaginative, and full of personality. The environments have a storybook-like quality that makes exploring them genuinely enjoyable.\n\nThere's a great contrast between the bright, welcoming areas and some of the darker elements of the story.\n\nThe art direction gives Pankapu its own identity, and it's one of those games where you can immediately recognize it from a screenshot.\n\n🗺️ Exploration is rewarding\n\nThe levels aren't just straight lines from point A to point B.\n\nThere's plenty of reason to explore, look around, and investigate areas that you might otherwise walk past.\n\nFinding secrets and collectibles gives you another reason to revisit areas and pay attention to your surroundings.\n\nI always appreciate platformers that reward curiosity instead of simply pushing you toward the next checkpoint.\n\n📖 A surprisingly interesting story\n\nOne thing I didn't expect going into Pankapu was how much I would enjoy the story.\n\nUnderneath the colorful presentation is a narrative with some surprisingly darker and more emotional themes.\n\nThe contrast between the cheerful visual style and the more serious elements of the story works really well.\n\nIt gives the adventure more meaning than simply running from one level to the next.\n\n🎮 Classic platforming fun\n\nThe platforming feels good and fits nicely with the combat and exploration.\n\nThere are plenty of moments where you need to time your movements, avoid hazards, and figure out how to reach certain areas.\n\nIt's not trying to reinvent the platformer genre, and honestly, it doesn't need to.\n\nSometimes you just need solid controls, fun levels, interesting abilities, and a world worth exploring.\n\nPankapu delivers all of that.\n\n✨ A game with personality\n\nWhat I enjoyed most is that Pankapu doesn't feel generic.\n\nThe characters, environments, art style, music, and story all work together to create something with its own identity.\n\nIt feels like playing through an interactive fantasy storybook, except you're also running around hitting monsters with a sword.\n\nWhich is obviously an excellent combination.\n\n🏆 Final verdict\n\nPankapu is a charming and enjoyable action-platformer that combines colorful visuals, fun combat, exploration, platforming, upgrades, and an unexpectedly thoughtful story.\n\nIt's the kind of game that's easy to recommend if you enjoy indie platformers and want something that feels colorful and approachable while still having some depth underneath the surface.\n\nIf you're a fan of games like classic action-platformers, colorful fantasy adventures, or simply want something fun and relaxing to play, give Pankapu a chance.\n\n⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐ Highly Recommended!\n\nGreat visuals.\n\nFun combat.\n\nInteresting world.\n\nA surprisingly meaningful story.\n\nAnd enough secrets to keep you looking around every corner.\n\nPankapu is a lovely little adventure — charming on the outside, with more going on underneath than you might expect. ⚔️🌈✨\n\n\nI hope this review has been helpful.",
